# The signing key for session cookies, generated on first run.
.env

# Workspaces: evidence vaults and their databases never belong in git.
workspace/
workspace-*/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
vault/

# Generated reports
keeneye-*-report.pdf

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real case material. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# The rules above already cover the vault, the database and .env, but they do
# not catch loose source documents — a folder of real files dropped anywhere
# else would be committed. These are the names people actually reach for, plus
# two explicit quarantine directories.
#
# Put anything real in private/ or incoming/, or keep it outside the repo.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignoring *.pdf / *.jpg wholesale: docs/screenshots/ is
# tracked, and a rule that broad gets switched off the first time it is
# inconvenient, which is worse than a narrower rule people trust.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
private/
incoming/

# Any DIRECTORY whose name mentions a case, evidence or exhibits — the trailing
# slash matters, so tracked files like evidencemode.js and 04-case-web.png are
# unaffected. Broad on purpose: "cases", "my-cases", "casefile-2026-014" and
# "case-2026-014" are all names a person actually types under pressure, and a
# pattern that misses one is a pattern that leaks.
*case*/
*evidence*/
*exhibit*/
# Title-case variants. git is case-sensitive on Linux and macOS, and "Evidence"
# is exactly what someone names a folder in Windows Explorer.
*Case*/
*Evidence*/
*Exhibit*/
